            "description_text": "<p>Unlike more conventional crops, truffles demand a set of conditions that you cannot “fix” later with more fertilizer, more water, or more effort. Climate, long-term climate stability, soil structure and chemistry, water access, and even neighboring trees all influence whether a site can ever become a productive truffle orchard.</p><p>ATC has translated decades of truffle climate and cultivation data into practical tools to evaluate candidate properties in North America. Foremost among these tools is the <strong>Advanced Truffle Climate Map</strong>, which can help you precisely target your land search to focus on areas with the ideal climate for truffles.</p><p>Our goal is simple: help you avoid unsuitable land and focus your search where a truffle orchard is actually worth considering.</p>"
